[
  {
    "sha": "6716fad19583a9a8cfafe45826058a8e2754ef3b",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDY3MTZmYWQxOTU4M2E5YThjZmFmZTQ1ODI2MDU4YThlMjc1NGVmM2I",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T04:57:37Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T04:57:37Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(pick): box-select edge chains and faces into an operation's picks\n\nCtrl (or Shift) + left drag in the viewport, in Edge or Face mode with an\noperation open, draws a rubber band instead of orbiting. Its release adds\nevery visible feature edge chain (Edge mode) or welded face (Face mode)\nin the box to the operation's picks as one SetOperationGeometry - one\nundo step. A drag to the right is a window (wholly inside), to the left\na crossing box (inside or touching). The #692 one pick rule holds:\nfeature chains only, and a candidate counts only if part of it is\nunoccluded from the eye (the click pick's own sight test); stock and\nfixtures are never candidates but still occlude.\n\nThe rule is app::pick::box_pick (box_bodies / box_select /\nbox_select_top); the gesture is ui::box_pick. MCP twin: pick_in_box, a\nworld X/Y box seen from straight above.\n\nDecisions: docs/decisions/979-box-select-picks.md.\n\nFixes #979\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
